 3 Strength

Weight: 0~
@174  = ~Gond, god of invention and artifice, is a deity rarely worshipped by traditional adventurers. Some thieves, however, revere Gond for his role in the development of locks, traps, and other complex machines. One such thief was the burglar Jurmar the Calm, who began his career as a locksmith. Known for his cool demeanor and steady hand, Jurmar paid priests of Gond to fashion this tool belt for him. Whenever Jurmar was stuck in a situation where he didn't have the right tool for a job, one of the small pouches on the belt would supply him with what he needed.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: +10%
– Find Traps: +5%
– Set Traps: +10% (Artificers only)

Weight: 2~
@175  = ~Minerva's Lucky Knucky Pendant~
@176  = ~Minerva's 'Lucky Knucky' was carved from the remains of a large knucklehead trout. Though certainly not the first option to come to mind as a worn accessory, scrimshaw has an earthen, natural beauty of its own. Minerva insists that it will bring its holder good luck.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Luck: +1
– Saving Throws: +1

Weight: 1~
@177  = ~Gond, god of invention and artifice, is a deity rarely worshipped by traditional adventurers. Some thieves, however, revere Gond for his role in the development of locks, traps, and other complex machines. One such thief was the burglar Jurmar the Calm, who began his career as a locksmith. Known for his cool demeanor and steady hand, Jurmar paid priests of Gond to fashion this tool belt for him. Whenever Jurmar was stuck in a situation where he didn't have the right tool for a job, one of the small pouches on the belt would supply him with what he needed.

Oswald has managed to add even more tools for the belt, further enhancing its usefulness.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: +15%
– Find Traps: +10%
– Set Traps: +20% (Artificers only)

Weight: 2~
@178  = ~Nauseated~
@179  = ~Empowered~
@180  = ~Gear Crash~
@181  = ~Gear Crash
(Evocation)

Level: 1
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: Neg.

A gear-shaped mass of energy originating from the plane of Mechanus is formed above the targeted creature, smashing into them and dealing 6d6 damage (half magical, half physical). If the target fails a Saving Throw vs. Spells, they are additionally Stunned for 1 round.~
